                    "q": "Write a cause and effect essay on 'Lavish spendings on weddings'. (Model essay, four paragraphs.)",
                    "a": "In our society, people spend a lot of money on weddings. They arrange big functions, serve many dishes and invite hundreds of guests. This lavish spending has become a fashion, but it causes many problems. The main cause of lavish spending is the desire to show off wealth and social status. People want to impress their relatives and friends. Another cause is social pressure; people fear that others will laugh at them if their wedding is simple. As a result, many families fall into debt. Poor families borrow money and spend years repaying it. Sometimes, parents cannot arrange the marriages of their daughters because they cannot afford such grand weddings. To solve this problem, we should keep weddings simple. The government should fix a limit on guests and dishes. People should spend money on the future of the couple instead of wasting it on show. In conclusion, simple weddings are better for families and for society."
