                "q": "1. Multiple Choice Question M.C.Qs. Spot the correct option.\n(i) The system of measurement in which angle is measured in radian is called: (a) CGS System (b) Sexagesimal (c) MKS system (d) circular system\n(ii) The union of two non-collinear rays at common vertex is called: (a) an angle (b) a degree (c) a minute (d) radian\n(iii) 10° = ______: (a) 600″ (b) 3600″ (c) 600′ (d) 600\n(iv) [[5π/4]] radians = ______: (a) 115° (b) 225° (c) 135° (d) 45°\n(v) ([[1/2]]) sec45° = ______: (a) √2 (b) [[√2/2]] (c) [[2/√2]] (d) [[1/2]]\n(vi) cosecθ · sinθ = ______: (a) 1 (b) 0 (c) −1 (d) 0.5\n(vii) sec²θ − tan²θ = ______: (a) 0 (b) 1 (c) −1 (d) cos²θ\n(viii) In unit circle for point (x, y), sinθ = ______: (a) x (b) −x (c) y (d) −y\n(ix) If sinθ = [[−1/√2]] and θ lies in the 3rd quadrant, then tanθ = ?: (a) −1 (b) 1 (c) ±1 (d) [[1/√2]]\n(x) If an object is above the level of an observer then angle formed between the horizontal line and observer's line of sight is called: (a) an angle of depression (b) an angle of elevation (c) an obtuse angle (d) None of these"
