                "q": "2. Akram started a business with Rs 70,000. After 3 months Aslam joined the business with Rs 40,000 and after 6 months Asghar also invested Rs 40,000. At the end of the year they earned a profit of Rs 28,800. Find the share of each partner in the profit.",
                "a": "Akram's effective investment = Investment capital × Time period\n= 70,000 × 12 = Rs 840,000\nAslam's time = 12 − 3 = 9 months\nAslam's effective investment = 40,000 × 9 = Rs 360,000\nAsghar's time = 12 − 6 = 6 months\nAsghar's effective investment = 40,000 × 6 = Rs 240,000\nRatio of effective capitals:\nAkram : Aslam : Asghar\n840,000 : 360,000 : 240,000\n84 : 36 : 24\n7 : 3 : 2\nSum of ratios = 7 + 3 + 2 = 12\nTotal profit = Rs 28,800\nAkram's share = [[7/12]] × 28,800 = Rs 16,800\nAslam's share = [[3/12]] × 28,800 = Rs 7,200\nAsghar's share = [[2/12]] × 28,800 = Rs 4,800"
